  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LAGUNA MADRE WETLANDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project area is at Rancho Los Ebanos and Laguna La Nacha within the Laguna Madre and the Rio Grande Delta Wetland Complex-- Mexican Federal Protected Area, San Fernando County, Tamaulipas, in northeastern Mexico. The Laguna Madre is one of the most important sites on the Gulf of Mexico for wintering migratory birds; over 130 bird species have been recorded in the area, including 15% of all waterfowl migrating to Mexico and more than 100,000 shorebirds. This wetland complex contains a large area of lakes that host waterfowl species like Redheads and Northern pintails that depend on drinking freshwater to dilute the salts consumed when feeding on the sea grasses of the Laguna Madre. The project will: 1) protect or restore more than 7,000 acres and develop a sustainable management plan for Rancho los Ebanos; and conduct a hydrology study and waterfowl monitoring across more than 8,000 acres.</narrative>
  </description>
